          "text": "**Answer: it dies almost immediately \u2014 one leg absorbs it, and the aircraft is back on schedule by the PHX turn.**\n\nWhat actually happened on N8633A that day: 3851 PHX\u2013SFO pushed 142 (all coded NAS, 141 min) and arrived 141 late at 20:26Z, and the delay then rode the tail through five more legs, every one of them carrying a late_aircraft charge:\n\n| leg | sched dep (UTC) | dep delay | late_aircraft |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|4106\\|SFO\\|PHX\\|1055 | 18:55 | 144 | 133 |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|172\\|PHX\\|LGB\\|1440 | 21:40 | 135 | 128 |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|65\\|LGB\\|LAS\\|1545 | 23:45 | 140 | 124 |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|65\\|LAS\\|DAL\\|1735 | 01:35 | 144 | 116 |\n| 2026-01-03\\|WN\\|65\\|DAL\\|HOU\\|2255 | 04:55 | 155 | 114 |\n\nIt cleared overnight at HOU: 2026-01-04|WN|2999|HOU|STL|0500 went out 3 minutes late.\n\nCounterfactual at 20 minutes, walking next_leg with a 35-minute minimum turn (5th-percentile WN ground time at SFO, 139 qualifying turns; PHX is also 35):\n\n- **3851 PHX\u2013SFO**: dep 16:15Z, arr 16:15 + 130 block = 18:25Z, 20 late.\n- **4106 SFO\u2013PHX**: earliest departure 18:25 + 35 = 19:00Z vs schedule 18:55Z \u2192 **5 minutes late**, arrives 21:00Z (sched 20:55Z), 5 late.\n- **172 PHX\u2013LGB**: earliest 21:00 + 35 = 21:35Z, schedule is 21:40Z \u2192 no push. Cascade stops here.\n\nSo the propagation is one leg deep and five minutes, versus five legs and 718 total departure-delay minutes as flown. The SFO turn is where it gets absorbed: scheduled ground there is 50 minutes (18:05 arr \u2192 18:55 dep), which swallows all but 5 minutes of a 20-minute inbound, and the PHX turn behind it has 45 minutes of scheduled slack.\n\nOne caveat on the turn assumption: the crew actually took 53 minutes on the ground at SFO (20:26Z arrival \u2192 21:19Z departure), not 35. If that 53-minute turn were unavoidable rather than a consequence of the late arrival, 4106 would go at 19:18Z, about 23 minutes late, and 172 PHX\u2013LGB would still depart on time (19:18 + 120 block = 21:18Z arrival, +35 = 21:53Z vs 21:40Z sched \u2014 that variant would push 172 by 13 minutes and then wash out at LGB, which has 40 minutes of scheduled ground). The data can't tell me which of those two turn times is the real constraint; that would need station staffing or gate data I don't have.",
          "type": "text"
        }
